# AWS Bedrock authenticates through the AWS default credential chain
# (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, ~/.aws profiles selected by
# AWS_PROFILE, or SSO) and takes its region from AWS_REGION, the profile,
# or `region` here. The wire protocol is per model: Claude speaks
# anthropic_messages, openai.* deployments speak responses, other
# OpenAI-surface models speak chat_completions, everything else converse —
# a per-model `protocol` overrides. Converse rejects non-off thinking
# configs; Claude thinking needs anthropic_messages. Model IDs are Bedrock
# model IDs or inference-profile ARNs.
#provider "amazon-bedrock" {
#  kind = "amazon-bedrock"
#  model "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-v2" { context_length = 200000 }
#  model "openai.gpt-4.1" { protocol = "responses" }
#}
